      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "\u2705 Metformin remains the standard first-line medication for type 2 diabetes, while SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 receptor agonists are typically prioritized as add-ons or first-line choices based on specific organ protection and weight goals.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 receptor agonists are typically prioritized as add-ons or first-line choices based on specific organ protection and weight goals"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udcca Comparing SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1s"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "\ud83d\uddd3 Administration: SGLT2 inhibitors are oral daily pills; most GLP-1s are weekly/daily injections."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "\ud83d\udcc8 A1C Reduction: GLP-1s lower A1C by up to 1.5%\u20132%; SGLT2 inhibitors lower it by about 0.7%\u20131%."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "\ud83d\udcc9 Weight Loss: GLP-1s achieve 4\u20136 kg loss; SGLT2 inhibitors achieve 1\u20133 kg loss."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "\ud83d\udca1 Heart & Kidneys: SGLT2 inhibitors excel in heart failure and chronic kidney disease; GLP-1s excel in stroke and major cardiovascular event prevention."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "\u26a0\ufe0f Side Effects: SGLT2 inhibitors risk genital/urinary infections; GLP-1s risk gastrointestinal upset (nausea, diarrhea)."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udccc Choosing the Right Option"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "\ud83e\udec0 Choose SGLT2 inhibitors if you have heart failure or chronic kidney disease."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "\u2696\ufe0f Choose GLP-1s if prominent obesity or atherosclerotic cardiovascular risk predominates."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you share your current A1C, kidney/heart status, and whether you prefer a pill or injection, I can help you evaluate which class fits your profile."
      }
    ],
